<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?><transcript><text start="1" dur="6.2">As a symbol of national renewal, today</text><text start="4.4" dur="5">we gather by the same runway that once</text><text start="7.2" dur="3.9">stood cracked [music] and silent</text><text start="9.4" dur="5.2">to announce that this very site will</text><text start="11.1" dur="4.9">soon be the premiere venue for the air</text><text start="14.6" dur="3">and space</text><text start="16" dur="3.65">demonstrations</text><text start="17.6" dur="3.8">from all over the world under the Trump</text><text start="19.65" dur="4.45">[music] administration.</text><text start="21.4" dur="4.9">Our ambition is back, our momentum is</text><text start="24.1" dur="4.6">back, our leadership is back, [music]</text><text start="26.3" dur="4.7">NASA is back, and above all, most</text><text start="28.7" dur="5.3">importantly, the United [music] States</text><text start="31" dur="5.6">of America is back. To the entire team</text><text start="34" dur="4.5">at NASA who have worked to make this</text><text start="36.6" dur="4.4">vision a [music] real reality, a</text><text start="38.5" dur="5.4">beautiful, a gorgeous reality,</text><text start="41" dur="4.2">congratulations [music] on this historic</text><text start="43.9" dur="2.62">achievement.</text><text start="45.2" dur="3">There could be no better place to</text><text start="46.52" dur="3.58">[music] launch the next generation of</text><text start="48.2" dur="4.3">American breakthroughs than Cape</text><text start="50.1" dur="4.4">Canaveral and the Kennedy Space Center</text><text start="52.5" dur="4.9">where America&amp;#39;s future [music]</text><text start="54.5" dur="2.9">will take flight.</text></transcript>